---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "APR vs Interest Rate: Why fees matter";
const description =
  "APR includes certain fees while interest rate does not. Learn how fees change the comparison. Educational use only.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/apr-vs-interest-rate-fees">
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">APR vs rate (fees)</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>APR vs interest rate: why fees matter</h1>
    <p>
      APR includes certain fees and can be higher than the nominal rate. This guide explains how fees change comparisons
      and when APR is the right metric.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/apr-vs-interest-rate">APR vs interest rate</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/apr">APR topic</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Why APR rises</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Fees reduce the net amount you receive.</li>
      <li>The payment stays the same, so the effective rate rises.</li>
      <li>APR captures some of those upfront costs.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Comparison checklist</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Keep the loan amount and term constant.</li>
      <li>Include all required upfront fees.</li>
      <li>Compare total dollars paid over your horizon.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Fee inputs to gather</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Origination, discount points, and underwriting fees.</li>
      <li>Any lender credits tied to a higher rate.</li>
      <li>Whether fees are paid upfront or financed.</li>
      <li>Third-party fees that do not count toward APR.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision checks</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare total dollars paid over your time horizon.</li>
      <li>Verify the net cash received after fees.</li>
      <li>Keep term and payment schedule consistent.</li>
      <li>Recalculate if you finance fees into the balance.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Expected payoff horizon or refinance timeline.</li>
      <li>Cash available to pay fees upfront.</li>
      <li>Impact of financing fees on loan-to-value.</li>
      <li>Lender credits versus permanent rate savings.</li>
      <li>Any prepayment penalties or lock conditions.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Fee timing</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Upfront fees hurt most when you keep the loan briefly.</li>
      <li>Financed fees raise the balance and total interest paid.</li>
      <li>Credits reduce cash-to-close but can increase lifetime cost.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Comparing APR across different terms.</li>
      <li>Ignoring financed fees that raise the balance.</li>
      <li>Choosing the lowest rate without checking total cost.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/apr-with-origination-fee">APR with origination fee</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/apr-when-fees-are-financed">APR when fees are financed</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Is APR always higher than the rate?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Often, but not always. If fees are low, APR can be close to the rate.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Does APR include all closing costs?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Not all costs are included. Review the disclosure to see which fees count.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/apr-calculator">Run APR comparisons</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/apr-when-fees-are-financed">APR when fees are financed</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/apr">APR topic</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-01-31</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
